@doc smysl/0.1 {
  id: v/f6
  intent: adversarial-corpus
  lang: en
  granularity: { profile: default }
  roots: [f/laundered]
}

@hypothesis h/guess { status: speculative }
~ The connection pool is probably the cause, on general principle.

@observation o/rumour { status: speculative }
~ Someone mentioned that the eu-west shard has been slow lately.

@claim c/laundered-once { status: derived, grounds: [h/guess] }
~ Pool saturation caused the latency regression in eu-west last Thursday.

The pool acquisition wait metric rose sharply during the same window as the
latency regression, and the two curves track each other closely enough that the
causal direction is not seriously in doubt among the people who looked at it.

@claim c/laundered-twice { status: inferred, grounds: [o/rumour] }
~ The eu-west shard has a systemic capacity problem across all services.

Reports of slowness in that region have accumulated over several weeks now, and
the pattern is consistent enough to point at capacity rather than at any one of
the individual services that happen to run there.

@finding f/laundered { status: derived, grounds: [c/laundered-once, c/laundered-twice] }
~ The eu-west capacity shortfall is the root cause of the auth regression.

Both the pool saturation and the broader capacity pattern point in the same
direction, and together they are enough to close the incident with capacity as
the identified root cause, plus a follow-up ticket for the region as a whole.
